# neural-decoder-bench

A controlled benchmark of neural decoders for quantum error correction.

Neural decoders are usually reported on their own codes, noise models and
training setups, so their results can't be compared directly. This repository
trains and evaluates them under identical conditions: same circuits, same
noise, same training budget, same test shots. It scores each decoder on
accuracy, decoding speed and training cost.

**Core study:** Cascade and a GNN decoder on the rotated surface code and the
[[144,12,12]] Gross code (with [[72,12,6]] for development), under uniform
depolarizing and SI1000 noise. Tesseract and Relay-BP are the references.
See [`docs/PLAN.md`](docs/PLAN.md).

## Status

| Component | State |
|---|---|
| Circuits (surface d3/5/7, BB [[72,12,6]], [[144,12,12]], X and Z) | done |
| Noise models: uniform, SI1000 (reproduces the reference circuits exactly) | done, tested |
| Seeded sampling, train/val/test seed splits | done, tested |
| Reference decoders: PyMatching, Tesseract (paper presets), Relay-BP | done |
| Evaluation runner (paired shots, Wilson CIs, provenance) | done, tested |
| Cascade | Phase 2 (stub with spec) |
| GNN | Phase 3 (stub with spec) |

## Setup

Python 3.11 or 3.12 (sinter does not build on 3.13 yet).

```bash
uv venv -p 3.12 .venv && source .venv/bin/activate
uv pip install -e ".[baselines,dev]"
pytest                 # fast tests (~5 s)
pytest -m slow         # reference decoders on BB codes (minutes)
```

Evaluate a reference decoder on one cell:

```bash
python scripts/eval_reference.py --decoder relay_bp --code bb72 --noise si1000 \
    --p 0.002 --max-shots 2000 --out results/reference.jsonl
```

## Layout

```
src/ndbench/
  circuits/   fixed circuit set (noiseless, vendored) + library.noisy(code, noise, p)
  noise/      uniform and SI1000 noise models
  codes/      BB code check matrices (for the Cascade torus layout)
  data/       seeded Stim sampling, seed splits
  decoders/   common interface; PyMatching, Tesseract, Relay-BP wrappers
  models/     Cascade, GNN (and optional transformer)
  eval/       runner, statistics
configs/      experiment grid
scripts/      CLI entry points, circuit vendoring
docs/         PLAN.md, decisions.md
tests/        pytest suite (+ reference SI1000 circuits)
```

## Conventions

- A **cell** is (code, basis, noise, p). Test shots for a cell come from a fixed
  seed, so every decoder sees the same shots.
- **LER** is reported per shot, per round, and per round per logical qubit.
  A shot fails if any logical observable is wrong.
- Every result row records the decoder settings, seed, git commit and package versions.

## Credits

Circuits are derived from [quantumlib/tesseract-decoder](https://github.com/quantumlib/tesseract-decoder)
(Apache-2.0); see `NOTICE`.
